{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The eighth month in the second year
The word of the Lord [B]came near
To Zechariah son of [C#]Iddo
He heard the spirit's quiet [D#m]load
The Lord was furious with your fathers
They did not listen to the prop[B]hets
But my words overtook [C#]your fathers
They repented in their own disas[D#m]ters
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[B]Return to me declares the Lord
And [C#]I will return to you [D#m]once more
Do [B]not be like your fathers now
[C#]Turn from your evil ways and [A#]vow
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The measuring [D#m]line will be stretched [B]out
Over Jeru[C#]salem in this [D#m]hour
My house will be rebuilt [B]there
The Lord of [C#]hosts declares it [D#m]fair
My [B]cities will overflow [C#]with prosperity
The [A#]Lord will comfort Zion free[D#m]ly
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
In the night I had a vision
A man on a red horse's [B]mission
Standing among the myrtle [C#]trees
The angel spoke to me with [D#m]ease
Patrolling the earth at rest and peace
Seventy years of anger [B]cease
The Lord answered with kind [C#]words
Comfort for the broken and [D#m]blurred
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[B]Jealous for Jerusalem with burning fire
An[C#]gry with the nations that are [D#m]near
[B]I have returned with mercy to the land
My [C#]people shall be safe and [A#]stand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
The measuring [D#m]line will be stretched [B]out
Over Jeru[C#]salem in this [D#m]hour
My house will be rebuilt [B]there
The Lord of [C#]hosts declares it [D#m]fair
My [B]cities will overflow with [C#]prosperity
The [A#]Lord will comfort Zion free[D#m]ly
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Four horns that scattered Judah fell
[B]Four craftsmen came to break them
[C#]Joshua stood in filthy clothes
[D#m]The angel spoke of holy hopes
Take the guilt away from you
[B]Clothe you in fine robes anew
I am [C#]going to bring the Branch
A [D#m]sign for your strength
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The plumb line in the hand of Zerubbabel
[B]Grace [C#]grace to the [B]capstone
[D#m]The eyes of the Lord range through the [B]earth
[C#]He sees the heart of the [D#m]man
{end_of_verse}

